              {
                "annotations": [],
                "text": "An analysis of the training examples reveals the following rule:\n- There is a green pixel (`3`) and a yellow pixel (`4`).\n- The green pixel (`3`) takes one step towards the yellow pixel (`4`) using Chebyshev / 8-directional movement:\n  - $\\Delta r = \\text{sign}(r_4 - r_3)$\n  - $\\Delta c = \\text{sign}(c_4 - c_3)$\n  - New position of `3`: $(r_3 + \\Delta r, c_3 + \\Delta c)$\n- The old position of `3` becomes `0`.\n- If the new position of `3` coincides with `4`, `3` overwrites `4`. Otherwise, `4` remains at its original position.\n\nPlease provide the test input grid.",
